# Club & Grub - World 9, stage 3: "Chieftains' Pyre" (designer D9b, Book II "The Far Shore"). The final boss stage.
# Difficulty 10, Expert only (DESIGN.md A.2 / A.3 / A.6 / B.6, GAMEPLAY.md 13.6). A short climb of 24 rows up the
# spire's flank past the Tar Tribe camp: the bottom terrace walked to the left (a tar pit, a tar wade, two tribesmen
# on lookouts), a vine to the middle terrace walked to the right (checkpoint 1, the camp: tents, huts, drums, a tar
# puddle, three tribesmen), a vine to the upper terrace walked to the left (the chieftains' tent hides Cave Painting
# 16 in its big spot, checkpoint 2, the Guard), the gallery under the summit and a chimney with two log grates that
# lead up into the pyre hall, one way. The hall (zones/arena, cols 24-43, rows 0-10, the side walls included; the
# camera locks on it): the carved floor (row 11) open to both side walls (the Roc perches of the roast thieves), two
# ledges and the altar of the Great Roast 3 rows up at the centre over the pyre, nothing standable higher, under a
# 5-row rock crown whose underside is 80 px under the view's top - so no standing or jumping chieftain is ever drawn
# under the HUD band (G35: a chieftain on the altar has his top 93 px under the view top). Gorm starts on the floor,
# Gulla waits on the altar by the roast (solo: they tag in one at a time); they run on hero physics over the bot graph
# resources/bots/w9_l3.json (core-B's baker, clipped to the hall). Their trophy, the Great Roast, leads to ending_b.
# Nothing needs a special.

[meta]
format = 2
id = w9_l3
name = "Chieftains' Pyre"
kind = main
order = 160
book = 2
world = 9
stage = 3
biome = sky
terrain_a = sky/terrain_rock
terrain_b = ruins/terrain_carved
background = pyre
music = level_pyre
liquid = tar
min_difficulty = expert
next = ending_b
password_expert = "PYR3"
bonus_tier = 2
author = D9b

